Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: More independent browser jobs without quality or coverage loss.
Dependencies: 71_FULL_RESOLUTION_RENDERING.todo.

Purpose
-------
Reduce sequential browser work per hosted runner while preserving native
timing, full-resolution rendering and every deployment gate.

Tasks
-----
[x] Inspect actual prior job timings and documented runner limits.
[x] Increase isolated browser shards from ten to nineteen, one worker each.
[x] Prove every current case is assigned exactly once.
[x] Remove duplicate fullscreen-frame waits without removing assertions.
[ ] Qualify the genuine pushed workflow and record observed elapsed time.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
All53 browser cases run once, fifteen shards of3 and four shards of2.
Nineteen browser jobs plus build fit the20-job baseline concurrency budget.
Native tests do not compete on the same runner. Rendering stays sharp.
No tests, assertions, deadlines, failure evidence or deployment gates removed.
Do not claim a controlled speedup from one hosted run or assume account limits.

